{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1531808-better-ghoul-clan-merits","id":1531808,"title":"Better ghoul clan merits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-01T14:28:48-08:00","id":1531808,"title":"Better ghoul clan merits?","content":"There are ghoul clan merits for each clans: Taste of Shadow (\u2022\u2022), Taste of the Serpent (\u2022\u2022), Taste of the Wild (\u2022\u2022), Taste of Gold (\u2022\u2022) and Taste of Fear (\u2022\u2022). While Taste of Fear and Taste of Serpent allow to impose a condition on other characters (fear of swooning), Taste of Wild allows creation of animal ghouls, and Taste of Shadow allows supernaturally gain information about Kindred and their influence, the Taste of Gold seems quite weak: it allows to gain another Vice, which recovers willpower in competitive situations. Somehow, this seems to me to be inferior to other merits. Do you agree? Do the other merits seem balanced?<br /> <br /> Do you have any &quot;homebrew&quot; merits for ghouls based on clans you would share? Something that would differentiate ghouls of different clans?<br /> <br /> Additional question: I own the Ghouls resource book, but it was created for the 1e Vampire: The Requiem 2004. Are there any errata or rules update for the resource book?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T03:16:05-08:00","id":1531840,"title":"","content":"Knowing someone's vice gives fairly decent advantages in social situations where you can offer to help them fill it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T10:51:22-08:00","id":1531847,"title":"","content":"But it gives you an extra V\u00edce, it does not read V\u00edce of the other party. <br /> <br /> &gt; Effect: Beating someone in competition is considered a second Vice for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T11:17:03-08:00","id":1531848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1531808-better-ghoul-clan-merits#post1531808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are ghoul clan merits for each clans: Taste of Shadow (\u2022\u2022), Taste of the Serpent (\u2022\u2022), Taste of the Wild (\u2022\u2022), Taste of Gold (\u2022\u2022) and Taste of Fear (\u2022\u2022). While Taste of Fear and Taste of Serpent allow to impose a condition on other characters (fear of swooning), Taste of Wild allows creation of animal ghouls, and Taste of Shadow allows supernaturally gain information about Kindred and their influence, the Taste of Gold seems quite weak: it allows to gain another Vice, which recovers willpower in competitive situations. Somehow, this seems to me to be inferior to other merits. Do you agree? Do the other merits seem balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taste of Gold outright gives you an extra Vice in circumstances that Vampire already incentivizes the table to bring in by the fact that one of the Conditions the Predatory Aura can cause relates to them.<br /> <br /> Taste of Fear and Taste of Shadow both cost Willpower and involve a roll; Taste of Shadow is further limited to once per scene and provides somewhat niche questions, while Taste of Fear requires you to reveal a secret about yourself to the victim and sabotages your next Social action with them if it fails.<br /> <br /> Taste of the Serpent functionally makes doing the sort of things you'd do for Soft Leverage more effective but doesn't give you any special insight into what someone's Vice is.<br /> <br /> Taste of the Wild requires you to purchase animal ghouls as Retainers and manage their Vitae upkeep. Lest we forget, ghouls have a Vitae capacity equal to their Stamina and can only get Vitae from vampires.<br /> <br /> Taste of Gold functionally gives you an excuse to spend Willpower on competitive actions with the reassurance that you'll immediately get it back once per scene. That's huge for a ghoul that isn't likely to be taught the clan Discipline of their regnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T02:25:56-08:00","id":1531871,"title":"","content":"Thank you, you are probably right - I think I was overestimating the other merits. Also, we do not tend to play Virtue/Vice that much, but when you do it properly, I imagine it can be quite strong.(in comparion).<br /> <br /> Any pointers to the rule update for the Ghouls resource book? (Or any experience with updating another resource book? Do the parameters typically stay the same, or are there some things that need rebalancing in particular?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T08:57:55-08:00","id":1532085,"title":"","content":"I assume you have Half Dammed, it\u2019s the second edition ghoul book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:02:07-08:00","id":1532101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1531808-better-ghoul-clan-merits?p=1532085#post1532085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you have Half Dammed, it\u2019s the second edition ghoul book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this is exactly what I was looking for! Thank you! (I have the original Ghouls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T12:36:01-07:00","id":1532815,"title":"","content":"Glad to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}